WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.266 --> 00:00:14.324
Marcus Bell: Morning, both. Thanks for hopping on. Before we dig in, how's the week going over there?

2
00:00:14.784 --> 00:00:24.462
Kyle Brennan: Busy. We're in the middle of termite renewal season, so half my techs are running behind and I'm answering phones in the Durham office two days a week.

3
00:00:25.684 --> 00:00:35.225
Ashley Moore: Which is exactly why I wanted this call. The numbers are okay, but I want to make sure we're getting everything out of what we already pay for.

4
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:41.383
Marcus Bell: Let's start with volume. What are you seeing on tracked calls for the quarter?

5
00:00:41.956 --> 00:00:54.409
Ashley Moore: We did about 2,140 inbound calls across the six locations from July through September. Google Ads drove roughly 1,460 of those, the rest is organic and some direct mail.

6
00:00:54.813 --> 00:00:57.601
Marcus Bell: And how does that compare to last quarter?

7
00:00:58.049 --> 00:01:06.302
Ashley Moore: Up about eleven percent. Mostly the Raleigh and Cary numbers, which makes sense since we bumped budget there in August.

8
00:01:07.747 --> 00:01:12.206
Marcus Bell: Are the signals firing the way you'd expect on those calls?

9
00:01:12.463 --> 00:01:23.641
Ashley Moore: They're fine. Appointment booked and quote given are the two we watch, and those look right. I spot-checked a dozen transcripts last week and they matched up.

10
00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:30.463
Kyle Brennan: Yeah, no complaints there. Which, speaking of Google Ads, I need to bring something up.

11
00:01:30.877 --> 00:01:31.744
Marcus Bell: Go ahead.

12
00:01:32.955 --> 00:01:47.194
Kyle Brennan: CallRail sent me a quote last month, and it's noticeably lower than what we're paying you all. Their whole pitch is that conversions land in Google Ads the same day, and I can't tell whether that matters or it's just a sales line.

13
00:01:48.276 --> 00:01:53.483
Marcus Bell: How are things looking on your side with the Google Ads connection right now?

14
00:01:54.249 --> 00:02:03.807
Ashley Moore: From what I can see the conversions show up, it's just not instant. Usually I see yesterday's calls reflected by the next morning.

15
00:02:04.235 --> 00:02:18.560
Marcus Bell: Okay. So on the same-day piece, I don't want to guess at how we'd handle that. Let me take it back to the team and get you a straight answer on what's possible.

16
00:02:18.987 --> 00:02:30.308
Kyle Brennan: That's all I'm asking. I'm not looking to switch over a few dollars, but if they're genuinely faster and cheaper, I'd be silly not to at least ask.

17
00:02:31.402 --> 00:02:34.391
Marcus Bell: Understood. I'll follow up by Thursday with something concrete.

18
00:02:35.092 --> 00:02:48.404
Ashley Moore: While you're at it, can you also send over a quick rundown of who on our side can pull reports? Renee retired in September and her login is still floating around.

19
00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:54.695
Marcus Bell: Sure, I'll put together the user list with roles and send it with the follow-up.

20
00:02:55.882 --> 00:03:10.382
Kyle Brennan: Appreciate it. One other thing, and this is small. Can we push our QBR to the first week of February? January is our slowest month and I'd rather not tie up Ashley's morning.

21
00:03:10.774 --> 00:03:17.583
Marcus Bell: That works on my end. I'll send a calendar hold for the first Tuesday in February.

22
00:03:18.032 --> 00:03:29.601
Ashley Moore: Perfect. Oh, and tell whoever handles your invoices that the Raleigh address changed, we moved suites in the same building. The last one went to the old suite.

23
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.751
Marcus Bell: I'll get that to billing today.

24
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:41.440
Kyle Brennan: Did you all see the storm that rolled through Friday? Knocked out power at the Garner shop for about four hours.

25
00:03:42.146 --> 00:03:44.466
Marcus Bell: I heard about that. Everyone okay?

26
00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:50.783
Kyle Brennan: Fine, just a long day. The calls still came through, so that part worked.

27
00:03:51.614 --> 00:03:55.018
Marcus Bell: Good. Anything else on your list before we wrap?

28
00:03:56.232 --> 00:03:59.191
Ashley Moore: That's it for me. Thanks for making time.

29
00:04:00.055 --> 00:04:01.406
Kyle Brennan: Same here. Talk Thursday.

30
00:04:01.705 --> 00:04:03.500
Marcus Bell: Thursday it is. Thanks, both.
